  "term": "DRGs",
  "definition": "DRGs refers here to dorsal root ganglion stimulation, a neurostimulation procedure used to help control chronic neuropathic pain that has been hard to treat. It works by delivering stimulation through implanted electrodes and an internal pulse generator, with an external component also involved.",
